## Context

Ticket 0302 found and fixed the Mismatched→EXACT_CAPACITY_DIFF mapping bug in
`reconcile.py`. The fix is mechanical but the LP matcher has no fixture-driven
regression suite. The 10 hard cases identified in `exp1_mismatched_audit.csv`
(Nong Son 1, Na Dương 1, An Khánh 1 blocked at sim≈88.9 by the 90-threshold
because the cleaner leaves Vietnamese `đ` unstripped) show the matcher needs
human-verified ground truth to catch future regressions.

The discussion also surfaced a related issue: the cleaner normalises accented
Vietnamese names incompletely — `đ` stays as `đ` rather than being mapped to
`d`, which reduces similarity scores for legitimate reference↔system pairs
(see top-10 in audit). That is a separate ticket scope.

## Proposed design

Directory-based fixture collection:

```
tests/fixtures/lp_matcher/
  tp_alias/             # unaccented alias → accented reference
    reference.csv
    system.csv
    expected.csv        # two columns: reference_name, system_name
  tn_hallucinated/      # hallucinated plant → SYSTEM_ONLY
    ...
  near_miss_unit/       # unit-number veto prevents cross-unit match
    ...
  duplicate_resolve/    # LP 1:1 constraint: only one of two candidates wins
    ...
  mismatched_split/     # LP-forced below-threshold pair → 2 entries, not 1
    ...
```

`expected.csv` convention:
- Matched pair: reference_name=X, system_name=Y
- Reference-only: reference_name=X, system_name=""
- System-only:   reference_name="", system_name=Y

The test parametrises over all subdirectories, loads the three CSVs, runs
`aedist.reconcile.reconcile()`, and compares actual match pairs to expected.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `tests/fixtures/lp_matcher/` with ≥ 5 fixture directories
- [ ] `tests/test_lp_matcher_fixtures.py` — parametrised, all pass
- [ ] Fixture for the Mismatched-split case documents the 0302 fix
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes
